{
  "$comment": "Canonical, server-side mapping from a (questionId, optionCode) pair to a validated SignalMutation. This file is the ONLY authority that may turn a user's answer into a clinical signal. A client never sends a clinical signal; it sends questionId + optionCode and nothing else. Every entry below is DERIVED, not invented: the signal codes come from the answered question's own resolvesSignals/escalationSignals in question_catalog_v1.json, and the presence values come from the plain meaning of an exclusive single-choice option. No clinician participated in this project, so these entries are an engineering review artifact and must never be presented as clinical approval. A question with no entry here resolves to UNSUPPORTED_MAPPING: the answer is recorded, no signal is invented, and nothing can reach GREEN on it.",
  "contractVersion": "1.0.0",
  "mappingRuleVersion": "CANONICAL_ANSWER_MAPPING_V1_2026_08_06",
  "reviewStatus": "DEV_REVIEWED",
  "internalReviewStatus": "DEV_REVIEWED",
  "clinicalValidationStatus": "NOT_CLINICALLY_VALIDATED",
  "externalClinicalSignOff": "NONE",
  "unmappedAnswerBehaviour": "REJECT_AS_UNSUPPORTED_MAPPING",
  "mapperMayProduceOutcome": false,
  "derivationRule": "An option maps only to signals the question already declares in resolvesSignals or escalationSignals, and only to signal codes present in the triage rule registry. Stage disambiguation is left to the rules: HEAVY_VAGINAL_BLEEDING and HEAVY_POSTPARTUM_BLEEDING are both asserted, and PREG_RED_001 / POST_RED_001 are stage-scoped so only the correct one can fire.",
  "reviewNotes": [
    "Ordered severity options are mutually exclusive by construction, so choosing a lower band is read as an explicit negative for the higher band (BLEEDING_MODERATE implies HEAVY_*=ABSENT). This is the one inference in this file that goes beyond literal restatement and is the first thing a reviewer should challenge.",
    "UNSURE maps to UNKNOWN, never to ABSENT. 'I do not know' is not a negative finding.",
    "EPIGASTRIC_PAIN and SWELLING were declared by questions but missing from the rule registry, so those answers could never become signals. Both are now registry signals and are mapped. No rule reads them yet: they are collected for a future preeclampsia rule, and collecting them is not the same as acting on them.",
    "Q_GLOBAL_DANGER and Q_SAFETY_SELF_HARM exist so that emergency and self-harm signals are reachable deterministically. Before them, all 16 of those signals could only arrive via free-text extraction, so an LLM outage left the engine unable to detect any emergency at all.",
    "Q_GLOBAL_DANGER is single-choice while a person may have several danger signs at once. That is safe here because GLOBAL_RED_001 fires on ANY one of them, so naming the most prominent sign is enough to escalate. It is deliberately not treated as evidence that the unnamed signs are absent — only DANGER_NONE asserts ABSENT.",
    "Q_SAFETY_SELF_HARM maps its UNSURE option ('I would rather not answer') to UNKNOWN, never ABSENT. Declining to answer a self-harm question is not a denial.",
    "Q_PAIN_SEVERITY declares no signals and does not state a body region, so it is unmapped.",
    "Q_BP_IF_KNOWN is a measurement question and travels through measurements, not signals.",
    "Q_PREGNANCY_TEST, Q_GESTATIONAL_WEEK, Q_POSTPARTUM_DAY and Q_BABY_AGE_MONTHS resolve context fields, not clinical signals.",
    "Q_CLARIFY_* are routing questions handled by the target/intent resolvers and must never produce a clinical signal.",
    "Q_HEADACHE_SEVERITY closes the other half of PREG_RED_002 (severe headache AND visual disturbance), which no question previously resolved. HEADACHE_MILD asserts SEVERE_HEADACHE=ABSENT because the options are an exclusive severity ladder: reporting mild pain is reporting that it is not severe."
  ],
  "allowedProvenance": [
    "USER_REPORTED",
    "QUESTION_ANSWER",
    "MEASURED",
    "LLM_EXTRACTED_VALIDATED",
    "PROFILE_CONTEXT",
    "HEALTH_MEMORY_CONTEXT"
  ],
  "provenanceRules": {
    "$comment": "HEALTH_MEMORY_CONTEXT and PROFILE_CONTEXT describe remembered background, not what is happening now. They must never be merged as a current PRESENT signal until the user confirms it in the current session.",
    "mayAssertCurrentPresent": [
      "USER_REPORTED",
      "QUESTION_ANSWER",
      "MEASURED",
      "LLM_EXTRACTED_VALIDATED"
    ],
    "mayNotAssertCurrentPresent": [
      "PROFILE_CONTEXT",
      "HEALTH_MEMORY_CONTEXT"
    ]
  },
  "allowedPresence": [
    "PRESENT",
    "ABSENT",
    "UNKNOWN",
    "CONFLICTED",
    "UNAWARE_OR_UNMEASURABLE"
  ],
  "mappingEntryShape": {
    "$comment": "Shape every entry in 'mappings' must follow.",
    "questionId": "string, must exist in question_catalog_v1.json",
    "optionCode": "string, must be one of that question's options",
    "signalCode": "string, must exist in the triage rule registry signal catalog",
    "presence": "one of allowedPresence",
    "current": "boolean"
  },
